IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fca-nouns`
IMPORT `sgia-p1-definitions`

-- Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation -- LAYER 1, THE DEFINED TERMS.
--
-- The Act defines one term itself ("the time of discharge", s 2(2)) and labels one party ("the benefited party", s 2(4)(a)).
-- It uses four words that the Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) defines ("court", "Government", "party", "person").
-- Those four are NOT re-encoded here: the copy of the Interpretation Act's definitions module (sgia-p1-definitions.l4, copied
-- unchanged from Commons) is IMPORTed and its look-up `the definition of` is called.
-- The Act uses other words it does not define ("frustrated", "charterparty", "contract of insurance", "specific goods", "perished",
-- "valuable benefit", "expenses"); those are asked as facts in fca-nouns.l4.

§ `The terms this Act defines`

DECLARE `Term of the Frustrated Contracts Act` HAS
    term IS A STRING
    `what the Act makes it mean` IS A STRING
    `where the Act says so` IS A STRING

-- src:42 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), all sums paid or payable to any party
-- src:43 | in pursuance of the contract before the time when the parties were so
-- src:44 | discharged (referred to in this Act as the time of discharge) shall, in
@ref s 2(2) "the time of discharge" (src:42-44)
`s 2(2) definition of the time of discharge` MEANS
    `Term of the Frustrated Contracts Act` WITH
        term IS "the time of discharge"
        `what the Act makes it mean` IS "the time when the parties were so discharged, that is, discharged from the further performance of the contract for the reason given in section 2(1)"
        `where the Act says so` IS "s 2(2)"

-- src:72 | (a) the amount of any expenses incurred before the time of
-- src:73 | discharge by the benefited party in, or for the purpose of,
-- src:74 | the performance of the contract, including any sums paid
-- src:75 | or payable by him to any other party in pursuance of the
-- src:76 | contract and retained or recoverable by that party under
-- src:77 | subsection (3); and
@ref s 2(4)(a) "the benefited party" (src:72-77)
`s 2(4)(a) label for the benefited party` MEANS
    `Term of the Frustrated Contracts Act` WITH
        term IS "the benefited party"
        `what the Act makes it mean` IS "the party to the contract who has obtained the valuable benefit, that is, 'the party obtaining it' in the opening words of section 2(4)"
        `where the Act says so` IS "s 2(4)(a), by the label; s 2(4) opening words for the meaning"

-- src:43 | in pursuance of the contract before the time when the parties were so
-- src:44 | discharged (referred to in this Act as the time of discharge) shall, in
-- src:72 | (a) the amount of any expenses incurred before the time of
-- src:73 | discharge by the benefited party in, or for the purpose of,
@ref s 2(2), s 2(4)(a) (src:43-44) (src:72-73)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Term of the Frustrated Contracts Act`
`all the terms this Act defines` MEANS
    LIST
        `s 2(2) definition of the time of discharge`,
        `s 2(4)(a) label for the benefited party`

-- src:43 | in pursuance of the contract before the time when the parties were so
-- src:44 | discharged (referred to in this Act as the time of discharge) shall, in
-- src:72 | (a) the amount of any expenses incurred before the time of
-- src:73 | discharge by the benefited party in, or for the purpose of,
@ref s 2(2), s 2(4)(a) (src:43-44) (src:72-73)
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Term of the Frustrated Contracts Act`
`s 2(2) and s 2(4)(a) the term this Act defines` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN t YIELD t's term EQUALS word) `all the terms this Act defines`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the Act defines only the two terms above; any other word is not defined by it
        NOTHING
    WHEN t FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST t

-- src:42 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), all sums paid or payable to any party
-- src:43 | in pursuance of the contract before the time when the parties were so
-- src:44 | discharged (referred to in this Act as the time of discharge) shall, in
@ref s 2(2) "the time of discharge" (src:42-44)
GIVEN c IS A `Contract facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 2(2) the time of discharge` MEANS
    IF c's `the parties to the contract have for that reason been discharged from the further performance of the contract`
    THEN c's `the date the parties were so discharged`
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the time of discharge is "the time when the parties were so discharged"; where they were not discharged for the reason in s 2(1) the Act gives it no date
        NOTHING

-- The yes/no twin of the function above (a date cannot carry JUST FALSE).
-- src:42 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), all sums paid or payable to any party
-- src:43 | in pursuance of the contract before the time when the parties were so
-- src:44 | discharged (referred to in this Act as the time of discharge) shall, in
@ref s 2(2) "the time of discharge" (src:42-44)
GIVEN c IS A `Contract facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(2) there is a time of discharge` MEANS
    IF c's `the parties to the contract have for that reason been discharged from the further performance of the contract`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a definition: the time "when the parties were so discharged"): "the time when the parties were so discharged (referred to in this Act as the time of discharge)"
        JUST FALSE

§ `The words of this Act that the Interpretation Act 1965 defines`

-- The Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1) defines these four words that this Act uses.  They are looked up in the copied module, not re-encoded.
--   "court"      ss 2(3) to 2(7), 3(3), 3(4)
--   "Government" s 3(2)
--   "party"      ss 2 and 3 throughout (a "party" includes a company, association or body of persons)
--   "person"     s 2(7)
`the words of this Act that the Interpretation Act defines` MEANS
    LIST "court", "Government", "party", "person"

GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE Definition
`Interpretation Act s 2(1) the definition of a word this Act uses` MEANS
    IF elem word `the words of this Act that the Interpretation Act defines`
    THEN `the definition of` word
    ELSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): this word is not one this Act uses that the Interpretation Act defines
        NOTHING
